35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The transport costs are a significant variable, increasing drastically with distance. Also, whole-building lets carry a risk where the remaining members must cover the cost of any last-minute cancellations.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"Publicly run beds are quite cheap, but the reality of inland centers is concerning. Other clubs reported eight people to a room and very strict lights-out policies. That doesn't sound like a restful environment.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that the seniors think staying together in the evenings is the best way for different year-groups to bond. Also, cooking for ourselves takes a lot of time and effort from the people on duty.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Transport is consistently the biggest expense, especially when we travel far. Also, whole-building lets are risky because non-refundable deposits mean we pay for members who cancel late.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The attendance sheets are worrying. A fifth of the club didn't even show up last time, and most of them quit by winter. We need a place that actually makes people want to come and stay.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if attendance is that unstable, the risk of non-refundable deposits for a whole building becomes a serious financial burden for those who actually attend.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Minato, if we prioritize bonding in the evenings, we can't ignore the sleep quality. Cramming eight people into one room with strict rules will only leave everyone exhausted and irritable.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shion, that's true. I don't want anyone to be grumpy because they couldn't sleep. But if we don't stay together, we might miss those special bonding times the seniors mentioned.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Asuka, I agree. Given the attendance trends Takumi mentioned, a fixed-headcount quote is too dangerous. We cannot afford to let a few cancellations drive up the cost for everyone else.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Minato, exactly. If we don't fix the atmosphere and get people to actually bond, we're just going to keep losing members. We need a place where everyone stays together, but it has to be appealing.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we prioritize an appealing environment to boost attendance, we must ensure the cost doesn't become prohibitive. A local option would minimize the transport burden and the risk of financial deficits.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"A local option might be safe, but if the goal is to stop members from quitting, we need a quality experience. Cheap, crowded public beds are a recipe for exhaustion, not bonding.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I'm worried that if we choose a place where we have to cook for ourselves, the organizers will be too tired to enjoy the camp. It seems like a lot of work for just a few people.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, I agree. Adding a heavy administrative and labor burden on top of financial risks is unwise. We should prioritize a destination that is both budget-stable and manageable for the organizers.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"I don't care about the paperwork or the cooking if it means the club falls apart. If we just stay local or go somewhere boring, we're not solving the real problem of the year-groups not talking.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, I understand your concern for the club's health, but financial instability can be just as damaging. We must find a balance where the cost is fair and predictable for every single member.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, predictability is fine, but a ""fair"" price for a miserable experience is still a waste. If we prioritize the budget over sleep and comfort, we're just paying for another failed camp.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I just want everyone to be happy. If the organizers are too exhausted from cooking and planning, they might not be able to help the other members bond, which would be sad.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"We need to be realistic. If we choose a high-risk option and the budget fails again, it won't matter how ""appealing"" the destination was. Stability is the only way to ensure the camp is fair for everyone.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"Stability is just a fancy word for playing it safe while the club dies. If we don't take a risk to actually bring people together this time, we're just managing a decline. We need a real camp experience.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
