60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option C is far too risky. Between the high transport costs and the non-refundable deposit for a whole building, the financial burden on attending members would be unpredictable and potentially unfair.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Option A is out of the question. Based on what I found about inland centers, we'd be cramming eight people to a room. That's a guaranteed way to ensure everyone is exhausted by the final day.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option B seems safe, but I worry people will just go home and we'll miss those bonding evenings. However, Option C has meals provided, which would be so much kinder to the organizers than cooking ourselves.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option B is the only choice that guarantees financial stability. Option C's distance and fixed-headcount deposits are a recipe for another deficit, which we simply cannot afford this year.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Option B is a joke. If people just go home, we're not having a camp, we're just having extra practice. We need Option C; it's the only one that actually forces us to stay together and bond.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, forcing people to stay together is not worth the risk of a financial deficit. If we use Option C and people cancel, the remaining members will be unfairly penalized to cover the costs.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Takumi, while I agree that Option B lacks the ""camp"" feel, Option C is a gamble on a place we've never used. If the sleep quality there is as bad as the public centers, we've just spent more money to be exhausted.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Takumi, I really want us to bond too, but I'm worried about the people organizing everything. If we pick a place with too much work, they might get too tired to enjoy the camp with us.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, that's exactly why Option B is preferable. It removes the stress of cooking and the risk of financial failure. We can't prioritize ""bonding"" if the cost becomes a burden for the members.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, you're prioritizing a spreadsheet over the people! If we keep playing it safe with Option B, the club will just keep shrinking. We need a real environment where we actually live together to fix this.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, a spreadsheet represents the actual money members have to pay. If we choose Option C and the costs spike due to cancellations, we are not helping the club; we are creating a financial barrier that might drive more people away.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, you're right about the money, but @Takumi is right that Option B isn't a camp. However, Option A is a disaster for sleep. If we want a real experience, Option C is the only logical alternative, provided the beds are actually decent.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I'm still a bit torn. I really want everyone to bond like the seniors said, but I don't want the organizers to be exhausted. Option C sounds lovely because of the meals, but is it too far?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, it is too far. The transport costs alone would be a massive portion of the budget. We cannot gamble with the club's funds again just for the sake of a ""lovely"" location.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, you're so focused on the budget that you're ignoring the fact that people are quitting! A cheap camp that nobody wants to attend is a total waste of money. We have to go for Option C.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I cannot support Option C. The risk of an uneven financial burden on members is too high. Option B is the only logical choice that ensures fairness and stability for everyone's wallet. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shion,,"Option A is a non-starter due to the sleep quality, and Option B is barely a camp. If we want to avoid a repeat of last year's exhaustion, Option C is the only viable bet. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I really don't want the organizers to be overwhelmed like last year, and having meals provided in Option C would be such a relief for them. I'll vote for Option C.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I cannot ignore the financial risks. Option C is a gamble we cannot afford, and Option A is impractical. Stability and fairness must come first. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'm not letting this club die just because you're afraid of a deposit. If we don't actually stay together, we're failing the members. I'm voting for Option C!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
